Third-party components
----------------------
PawLink includes open-source components that remain under their own licenses.
Nothing above limits the rights these licenses give you for those components.

- mihomo (MetaCubeX)            GPL-3.0      source with PawLink changes: source/mihomo
- sing-tun (SagerNet)           GPL-3.0      source with PawLink changes: source/sing-tun
- gVisor (Google)               Apache-2.0   source: source/gvisor
- WDTT-Plus (Ivan4537)          GPL-3.0      source with PawLink changes: source/wdtt-plus,
                                             source/wdtt-android-client, source/wdtt-android-server
- PawLink Android core bridge   GPL-3.0      source/android-core (the part of libpawcore.so
                                             that is linked with mihomo)
- Twemoji Country Flags         CC-BY 4.0    flag font of the Windows application

The full license texts are in the corresponding folders under source/.
The GPL-3.0 text is available at https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.txt

Earlier versions of this repository published part of the Windows client under the
MIT license. That permission stays valid for exactly those earlier published files;
it does not extend to later versions.
